# Packages releng still lists that the repos no longer carry.
#
# build.sh copies upstream's packages.x86_64 verbatim, which is how this ISO
# tracks archiso for free — and how it inherits archiso's lag behind the repos.
# pacstrap resolves the whole list at once, so one dropped package fails the
# build with `error: target not found` and nothing else.
#
# One name per line, exact match, with why. build.sh says so when a line here
# is no longer in releng's list, which is the signal to delete the line.

# broadcom-wl: dropped from extra some time after 2026-08-28 (the v1.8.0 ISO
# built fine), leaving only broadcom-wl-dkms. dkms is not a substitute in a live
# image: nothing builds the module against the ISO's kernel at mkarchiso time,
# so it would not load in the live environment either way. Cost of dropping it
# is a machine whose *only* network is old Broadcom wifi, which then needs a
# cable to reach the installer. archiso 89-1.
broadcom-wl
